<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rundāle Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1736–1768</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rundāle Palace is a baroque palace in southern Latvia built from 1736 as the summer residence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernst-johann-von-biron">Ernst Johann von Biron</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a>, to designs by Francesco Bartolomeo Rastrelli. Work stopped when Biron was exiled in 1740 and was completed in 1768 after his return, with rococo interiors by Johann Michael Graff. It is now a museum and one of Latvia's best-known monuments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rundale-palace.jpg" alt="Rundāle Palace" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arian Zwegers · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rundale_Palace_(6483271573).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
